3. Instruction Set Architecture
3.1 Instruction Formats
LSX-64 defines 9 instruction formats, following the LoongArch taxonomy:
2R-type:   [ opcode(24) | Rj(5) | Rd(5) ]
3R-type:   [ opcode(16) | Rk(5) | Rj(5) | Rd(5) ]
4R-type:   [ opcode(10) | Ra(5) | Rk(5) | Rj(5) | Rd(5) ]
2RI8:      [ opcode(15) | I8(8)  | Rj(5) | Rd(5) ]
2RI12:     [ opcode(7)  | I12(12) | Rj(5) | Rd(5) ]
2RI14:     [ opcode(7)  | I14(14) | Rj(5) | Rd(5) ]
2RI16:     [ opcode(5)  | I16(16) | Rj(5) | Rd(5) ]
1RI21:     [ opcode(10) | I21(21) ]
I26:       [ opcode(6)  | I26(26) ]

* Rj, Rk are source register operands. Rd is the destination. Ra is an additional source for 4R-type (e.g., fused multiply-add).
* Immediate fields are sign-extended unless otherwise specified.
* 2RI16 is used for conditional branches (16-bit signed offset × 4).
* 1RI21 provides a 21-bit offset for unconditional branches (±1 MB range).
* I26 provides a 26-bit offset for long jumps (±128 MB range).
