5.3 Cache Operation
* L1 Instruction Cache (L1-I): Accessed in IF1–IF2 stages. On hit, instruction is available in IF2. On miss, the pipeline stalls until the line is fetched from L2 (or main memory).
* L1 Data Cache (L1-D): Accessed in MEM1–MEM2 stages. On hit, data is available in MEM2. On miss, stalls until line arrives from L2.
* L2 Unified Cache: Servs both I-cache and D-cache misses. 8-way set-associative with LRU replacement.
* Replacement: LRU (Least Recently Used) for all cache levels.
5.4 Memory Consistency Model
LSX-64 uses a total store order (TSO) memory consistency model for simplicity. All stores are committed to the cache hierarchy in program order. The DBAR instruction acts as a full memory barrier.
5.5 Address Translation (Specified, Not Simulated)
LSX-64 specifies a 4-level page table structure for virtual-to-physical address translation (48-bit virtual address space), with 4 KB page granularity. The TLB has 64 entries, fully associative. This is specified for completeness but the simulator operates on physical addresses directly.
  

