8. Design Rationale
8.1 Why No Delay Slots?
MIPS introduced branch delay slots to hide the branch penalty in early pipelines. However, as pipelines deepened, delay slots became a compiler burden and a source of wasted instructions. LoongArch eliminated them (LoongArch Reference Manual, Vol. 1), and RISC-V never included them. LSX-64 follows this modern consensus: no delay slots, relying on branch prediction (or simple predict-not-taken in the base model) to manage branch penalties.
8.2 Why 9 Instruction Formats?
LoongArch's 9-format design enables wider immediates and larger branch offsets than the 3-format MIPS design or the 4-format base RISC-V design. The trade-off is slightly more complex decode logic, but the benefit is improved code density (fewer instructions needed for large constants and far branches).
8.3 Why a 7-Stage Pipeline?
A 7-stage pipeline balances:
* Clock frequency: More stages = shorter logic paths = higher clock.
* Branch penalty: More stages = higher flush penalty on mispredict.
* Memory latency: Two MEM stages (MEM1, MEM2) accommodate L1 cache latency without blocking the EX stage for non-memory instructions.
The 3-cycle branch penalty (flushing IF1, IF2, ID/RF) is moderate for a 7-stage design and comparable to other in-order RISC pipelines.
  

9. Simulator Implementation Notes
The LSX-64 cycle-accurate simulator (lsx64_simulator.py) implements:
* Full fetch-decode-execute loop with 7-stage pipeline
* Register file with r0 hardwired to zero
* Hazard detection with EX-to-EX and MEM-to-EX forwarding
* Load-use stall (1 cycle)
* Branch penalty (3 cycles, predict-not-taken)
* Two-level cache hierarchy (L1 split, L2 unified) with LRU replacement
* Cycle counting for CPI, IPC, stall breakdown, and cache statistics
* A built-in assembler for writing test programs in LSX-64 assembly
The simulator does not implement:
* Out-of-order execution (the pipeline is in-order scalar)
* Branch prediction (predict-not-taken only)
* Floating-point operations
* Virtual memory / TLB
* Privileged mode instructions
* LSX-64BT (binary translation) instructions
  

